Prior efforts to tackle this have typically depended on extensive resources for generating data or demanded teachers who can supply detailed demonstrations encompassing actions, states, velocities, and accelerations. This work posits that leveraging the student's inherent capacity for understanding dynamics significantly enhances learning efficiency. By doing so, students internalize the task dynamics and reproduce optimal behaviors, even when their teacher provides data of limited quality. Specifically, this paper introduces a novel online strategy for demonstrating skills that overcomes the obstacles of noise and scarcity.

